mips: Ingenic XBurst2 hardware registers 4 and 8..12

XBurst2 (Ingenic T40/T41) answers rdhwr for registers the MIPS spec
leaves undefined, and its software uses them once HWREna enables them
(the soc-nna driver writes HWREna = ~0):

  $4       the physical address the last LL touched; the vendor kernels
           turn user addresses into physical ones with "ll; rdhwr $4"
  $8..$10  wait for the NNA DMA's read channels 0..2
  $11/$12  wait for its write channels 0..1 (Ingenic's libvenus,
           aie_wait_nndma_rdchn / wrchn)

On a CPU with ASE_MXU3 (XBurst2) HWREna keeps bits 4 and 8..12,
rdhwr $4 returns CP0_LLAddr and $8..$12 return 0 at once: the machine's NNA DMA model completes each
transfer when it is started.  Elsewhere they keep raising RI.

